    "C12","C02","C04","C05","C07","C13","C14","C17","C03","C06","C10","C11","C19","C09"
  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Direct human absolute oral bioavailability measurements in all visible L1 contexts are 43-91%, with no value below 20%; the most structurally relevant nitrile/fused-heteroaromatic contexts (glasdegib 77.12%, AG-221 57.2%, ondansetron 50-65%) support F≥20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C18","C21","C08","C15","C16","C01","C20","C12","C02","C04","C05","C07","C13","C14","C17","C03","C06","C10","C11","C19","C09"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L2 nonvoting records reinforce the same direction: vilazodone fed absolute BA is 72% (reported range 22-72% at 10-40 mg/day) and trazodone fasted/fed BA is 63-91%; even the lower bound of the vilazodone range is at/above the threshold.",
      "card_ids": ["C22","C23","C25","C28","C30","C33","C34","C29","C31","C26","C27","C24","C32","C35"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records do not provide a direct F measurement for the query, but the only oral-vs-IV comparison (tedizolid) shows high relative exposure (AUC 26.1 vs 30.5 µg·h/mL, ~86%), and anastrozole—which shares the query's 2-cyanopropan-2-ylphenyl motif—shows measurable steady-state oral AUC (median 37.4-42.9 µg·h/mL).",
      "card_ids": ["C54","C64","C43","C56","C40","C78"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "oral_auc_cmax_exposure",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C54","C64","C43","C56","C40","C78"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule itself.",
    "L3 records are mostly oral AUC/Cmax without IV comparator; they cannot quantify F for the query.",
    "Dose, formulation, and prandial state for the query are unknown; food effects and solubility-limited absorption cannot be excluded.",
    "No query-specific measurements of metabolic first-pass, efflux, or solubility; CYP3A/P-gp effects seen in unrelated L3 records (capmatinib, fexofenadine) are not directly transferable.",
    "Transfer from training contexts and L3 reference molecules is qualitative; no exact structural match is present."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L1/L2 direct human absolute BA values (43-91%) and L3 oral exposure records (including anastrozole with the same 2-cyanopropan-2-ylphenyl motif and tedizolid oral/IV AUC ratio ~86%) support F≥20%; no affirmative evidence of F<20% is present. The unfavorable solubility prior is a limitation but not endpoint proof, so the prediction remains high."
}

